<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xri version="1.0">
   <description><p>BlackRig scripts for PixInsight, by Erellaz.</p></description>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.9.0:2.0.0">
      <package fileName="SatelliteTrailRemover-3.0-20261118.zip" sha1="b33051220583c29a96e5ff4d81ce1103c188677e" type="script" releaseDate="20261118">
         <title>SatelliteTrailRemover</title>
         <description><p>SatelliteTrailRemover 3.0 and its WBPP step 1.4, by Erellaz (MIT license). New in 3.0: wide trails (the faint wings of bright trails are followed down to the noise and removed; on by default).</p><p>Removes satellite trails from registered light frames by comparing each frame with a trail-free stack of the same frames and subtracting only the trail. Runs on open frames, in batch, or as a step inside WeightedBatchPreprocessing.</p><p>After installing: Script &gt; BlackRig &gt; SatelliteTrailRemover. For WBPP, select src/scripts/BlackRig/SatelliteTrailRemover/SatelliteTrailRemover_WBPP.js in the PixInsight installation folder as WBPP's pipeline builder (Pipeline tab).</p><p>Documentation: SatelliteTrailRemover_quick_start.pdf in the same folder.</p></description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
